& [Inside_RIS_P0]
  + parse and validate one supplied strict runtime-closure request containing exactly one bootstrap-runtime root and one installation-SOP root
  + validate bounded material nodes prerequisites immutable sources producer edges portable logical targets and evidence references
  + derive reachability producer uniqueness acyclicity deterministic topological order target uniqueness unresolved prerequisites capability denials plan identity and expected-receipt identity
  + emit byte-deterministic effectless plan envelope and verification forms and independently reconstruct them from retained supplied bytes

& [Boundary]
  + a material declaration is not possession; a content hash is not provenance trust license compatibility safety availability or semantic suitability
  + closure compilation is not material resolution; resolution is not acquisition or build; expected layout is not a filesystem write; expected receipt is not an observation receipt; verification is not activation
  + an external-custody prerequisite may name a role and reference identity but never carries secret bytes

& [Outside_RIS_P1_P2_P3]
  + filesystem inspection creation mutation permissions links deletion rollback or cleanup
  + environment clock process shell compiler package manager network resolver provider model MCP Git workspace service runtime inference remote host or hardware contact
  + bootstrap binary selection distribution dependency vendoring artifact-pack construction license acceptance installation activation recovery upgrade successor recognition and physical receipt issuance

& [Outside_Unimported]
